manual.append(page('Updates and time synchronization',p('Use <b>Discover → Updates → Refresh</b> to review package updates. No updates after a day can be normal when the installed package set is already current.'),h('Verify the update path'),code('timedatectl status\nsudo apt update\napt list --upgradable'),p('Run each command in order. The first checks the clock. The second refreshes repository metadata without installing updates. The third lists upgrades available from configured APT sources.'),p('Expect a correct date/time, an active NTP service and synchronization when network time is reachable. A successful refresh should complete without fetch or signature errors. If APT reports all packages are up to date, no APT upgrade is pending from those sources.'),h('Install available updates'),p('Use Discover to review and install updates. If you prefer Konsole, run the commands below and review the proposed changes before accepting. Reboot when a kernel or other system update requests it.'),code('sudo apt update\nsudo apt upgrade'),h('Two different update channels'),p('Debian packages use the configured Debian repositories. JatayuOS-specific package changes committed to GitHub are not automatically delivered by those repositories. This version has no separately configured signed JatayuOS update repository.'),h('If refresh fails'),p('For “not valid yet”, check the clock and network time. For download errors, check connectivity and DNS. If another package manager holds the lock, let it finish. Do not delete lock files or disable signature checks to bypass an error.'),p('APT behavior reference: Debian Reference, Chapter 2. See the references page.')))
manual.append(page('Android language and personalization',h('Waydroid is optional'),p('The Waydroid package is included, but Android images require a separate initial download. JatayuOS remains usable without Android setup. This version does not bundle Google apps, Play Store or ARM translation libraries.'),p('Open Android Setup (Waydroid) to check readiness and read official instructions. Wayland, binder support and suitable graphics are required. The container stays off at boot; start and stop it from this page when needed.'),code('echo "$XDG_SESSION_TYPE"\nwaydroid status'),p('Initialize using official Waydroid documentation. The package is already included from Debian backports. Then open Android Setup and choose Start installed Waydroid UI; authenticate when prompted. To open Android Setup from Konsole:'),code('jatayu android'),p('Official setup: <link href="https://docs.waydro.id/usage/install-on-desktops" color="#172A3D">docs.waydro.id/usage/install-on-desktops</link>'),h('Language and input'),p('English is the normal default, with explicit en_IN.UTF-8 locale settings. Configure optional Indian input methods and layouts through System Settings and Fcitx tools. A sign-out may be needed after input changes.'),code('locale'),h('Personalize the workspace'),p('Change display scaling, keyboard shortcuts, panel settings and appearance through System Settings. Test small changes first, especially in a VM. Use Wallpaper Changer for the bundled offline collection.')))
manual.append(page('Troubleshooting and support',*table(['Symptom','First check'],[['No available updates','Refresh APT successfully before interpreting an empty list'],['APT says not valid yet','Verify date time and network synchronization'],['Dolphin previews missing','Enable previews and check file type size and settings'],['Launcher needs repeated clicks','Compare physical button tap-to-click and an external mouse'],['Silent audio','Select the correct output and check mute state'],['Wallpaper does not change','Check current KDE Activity target display and app message'],['Waydroid will not start','Check Wayland initialization binder and graphics support']],[176,328]),h('Collect a useful report'),code('cat /etc/os-release\nuname -r\nfree -h\ndf -h /\ntimedatectl status'),p('Record the exact action, expected result, actual result and whether it happens in a live or installed session. For a VM, include VM software, RAM, CPU count and graphics settings. Include the ISO source SHA or checksum if available.'),p('For recent service errors, you can inspect the command below. Review the text and screenshots for usernames, network details or other private information before sharing them.'),code('journalctl -b -p warning --no-pager -n 80'),h('Backups'),p('Keep important files on another device. If you use Jatayu Sanjeevani, it makes personal-folder backups and restores into a new folder; it is not a complete system image or bootable recovery service.'),p('Project website: <link href="https://jatayuos.in" color="#172A3D">https://jatayuos.in</link>. No guaranteed support response time is implied.')))
manual.append(page('About credits and references',h('About JatayuOS'),p('JatayuOS 1.0 Udaan is an independent India-made operating-system project by Anup Yadav, built on Debian 13 and KDE Plasma. Its identity uses the Jatayu name and eagle imagery; the name evokes the Jatayu figure in the Ramayana. This is a naming explanation, not a claim of government affiliation.'),h('Credits and installed notices'),p('Debian, KDE and their contributors provide the base system and desktop. Mozilla provides Firefox; The Document Foundation and contributors provide LibreOffice. Calamares, Waydroid, Fcitx and many other upstream projects provide additional components. These contributors retain their own authorship and rights.'),p('Read installed package notices under /usr/share/doc. The image also includes /usr/share/jatayu/notices and build-package-manifest.tsv for package/source-version references. Original Jatayu software is GPL-3.0-or-later under the approved scope in COPYRIGHT.md. Bundled applications and artwork may have different terms; this manual does not replace them. The full GPL text is installed with the integration copyright notice.'),h('Documentation sources'),p('Project source and configuration reviewed: <link href="https://github.com/jatayuos4u/jatayuos" color="#172A3D">github.com/jatayuos4u/jatayuos</link>. Relevant files include apps/app.py, apps/webapp.py, docs/DUAL-BOOT.md, docs/UPDATES.md and docs/COMPLIANCE.md. Repository visibility depends on project access.'),p('Debian package management: <link href="https://www.debian.org/doc/manuals/debian-reference/ch02.en.html" color="#172A3D">Debian Reference Chapter 2</link>.<br/>Waydroid: <link href="https://docs.waydro.id/usage/install-on-desktops" color="#172A3D">Official desktop installation instructions</link>.'),h('Screenshot and validation scope'),p('All ten figures come from the owner’s supplied VM captures. Originals are embedded losslessly and fitted to the page; no UI controls, status values or features have been invented. The owner reported the new ISO’s observed problems resolved. That report does not establish universal hardware compatibility or every firmware/partitioning scenario.'),p('Dates, sample paths and labels in screenshots illustrate that captured session. Secure Boot, encryption, BIOS, Windows dual boot and Android app compatibility need scenario-specific verification. The guide preserves the testing capture provenance; it does not certify untested scenarios.')))
